Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3128: raise the LCDC QoS priority in arch_cpu_init

Mainline U-Boot has no RK3128 arch_cpu_init. The vendor loader raises the
LCDC AXI QoS priority to the highest level, and Linux keeps the QoS
register as the bootloader left it. On the Powkiddy A12 the priority
found before U-Boot (1/1) let CPU and GPU traffic starve LCDC scanout:
the RGB panel flickered with black vertical lines under memory load at
DDR 456 MHz. Writing the vendor value removes them.

The vendor function also sets the MSCH read latency, which already reads
0x3f before U-Boot on the A12, and muxes GPIO1C1 from sdcard_detn to GPIO.
On the A12 the GPIO1C1 write stops a cold power-on (warm reboots are
unaffected), alone or together with the other writes; neither is ported.

Comparison: caesar-u-boot 9724e7aa arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3128/rk3128.c
(arch_cpu_init). Existing GPL notices are retained.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3128/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3128/Makefile
@@ -6,3 +6,4 @@
 
 obj-y += syscon_rk3128.o
 obj-y += clk_rk3128.o
+obj-y += rk3128.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3128/rk3128.c
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
+/*
+ * Copyright (c) 2017 Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd
+ *
+ * LCDC QoS setting from the vendor caesar-u-boot 9724e7aa
+ * arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3128/rk3128.c arch_cpu_init.
+ */
+#include <init.h>
+#include <asm/io.h>
+
+#define QOS_LCDC_PRIORITY	0x1012f188
+#define QOS_PRIORITY_LEVEL(h, l) \
+	((((h) & 3) << 8) | (((h) & 3) << 2) | ((l) & 3))
+
+int arch_cpu_init(void)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Highest DDR priority for LCDC scanout. With the priority left by
+	 * the earlier boot stages (1/1) the Powkiddy A12 RGB panel shows
+	 * black vertical lines under memory load; Linux keeps the
+	 * bootloader's QoS setting.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor function also sets the MSCH read latency (already 0x3f
+	 * before U-Boot on the A12) and muxes GPIO1C1 (sdcard_detn) to GPIO.
+	 * The GPIO1C1 write stops a cold power-on of the A12, so neither is
+	 * ported.
+	 */
+	writel(QOS_PRIORITY_LEVEL(3, 3), QOS_LCDC_PRIORITY);
+
+	return 0;
+}
